classDiagram
    %% PawPal+ class design. Keep this file updated so it matches your final implementation.

    class Owner {
        +string name
        +int time_available
        +list~string~ preferences
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet) None
        +all_tasks() list~Task~
        +task_owner(task) Pet
    }

    class Pet {
        +string name
        +string species
        +string breed
        +string gender
        +int age
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task) None
        +complete_task(task, today) Task
        +describe() string
    }

    class Task {
        +string description
        +int time_minutes
        +string frequency
        +string due_time
        +bool required
        +string priority
        +bool completed
        +int anchor_day
        +date due_date
        +mark_complete() None
        +next_occurrence(today) Task
        +start_minutes() int
        +end_minutes() int
        +display_time() string
        +overlaps(other) bool
        +importance_level() int
        +priority_score() int
        +is_due_today(today) bool
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +int time_available
        +complete_task(task, today) Task
        +filter_tasks(pending_only, frequency, pet, due_on) list~Task~
        +sort_by_time(tasks) list~Task~
        +sort_tasks() list~Task~
        +detect_conflicts() list~tuple~
        +build_plan() list~Task~
        +explain_conflicts() string
        +explain() string
    }

    Owner "1" --> "*" Pet : owns
    Pet "1" --> "*" Task : has
    Scheduler "1" --> "1" Owner : plans for
    Scheduler ..> Pet : completes tasks via
    Task ..> Task : regenerates next occurrence
    note for Scheduler "tasks / time_available are derived from owner (single source of truth)"
